  <Docs>
    <summary>Provides an input event and its handled state for a TV interactive app view event handler.</summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>This .NET event data represents a call to <see cref="M:Android.Media.TV.Interactive.TvInteractiveAppView.IOnUnhandledInputEventListener.OnUnhandledInputEvent(Android.Views.InputEvent)" />. Read <see cref="P:Android.Media.TV.Interactive.TvInteractiveAppView.UnhandledInputEventEventArgs.Event" /> to inspect the input, and set <see cref="P:Android.Media.TV.Interactive.TvInteractiveAppView.UnhandledInputEventEventArgs.Handled" /> to control the listener's return value.</para>
      <para>The generated event adapter starts <c>Handled</c> at <see langword="true" /> when it invokes a subscribed handler. Set it to <see langword="false" /> if the handler does not consume the event.</para>
      <para>Based on the pinned <format type="text/html"><a href="https://github.com/dotnet/java-interop/blob/92b5d471f1e0f6164fc332b1f661b472f5cf3aad/tools/generator/SourceWriters/InterfaceEventHandlerImplClass.cs">.NET listener event generator</a></format>.</para>
    </remarks>
  </Docs>
